      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-51979",
      ":question/problem": "The concentration of a solution, measured in moles per liter ($mol/L$) varies inversely with the solution's volume, measured in liters ($L$). When the volume of the solution is $0.5L$, the concentration is $0.25mol/L$. Find the concentration of the solution when the volume is $0.1L$.\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question."
